cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived tables, please cite the accompanying manuscript and this repository."
title: "Pretreatment interferon activation and cytotoxic immune enrichment are associated with response to neoadjuvant chemoradiotherapy in locally advanced rectal cancer: a systematic multi-cohort transcriptomic meta-analysis"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
authors:
  - family-names: Wei
    given-names: Bizhi
    email: 15619056250wbz@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9481-3024"
    affiliation: "Puai Medical College, Shaoyang University"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bizhi-Wei/larc-ncrt-ifn-meta"
keywords:
  - rectal cancer
  - neoadjuvant chemoradiotherapy
  - interferon
  - transcriptomics
  - meta-analysis
  - GEO
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R pipeline for a systematic multi-cohort reanalysis of pretreatment
  bulk transcriptomes in locally advanced rectal cancer treated with neoadjuvant
  chemoradiotherapy. Nine nCRT cohorts (n=577) form the primary random-effects
  meta-analysis of interferon, cytotoxic-lymphocyte and NK-cell scores against
  pathological/clinical response; a radiotherapy-only cohort enters a
  treatment-scope sensitivity analysis.
